Not taken: tools/mesa/air/air_run.c (a test harness that draws on the Adreno), every .py tool,
prebuilt/ (binaries), the Panfrost, freedreno and ir3 patches (another GPU), tools/mesa/redwood-drm
(Jesvi's libdrm stand-in: on the A56 Mesa reaches the GPU through its Darwin vdrm), xnu/, and no
Apple metallib, shared-cache extract or capture.

What was changed, and why, is listed in "Changes" below (and in git history: the first commit is
the verbatim copy).

Changes
-------

Each change is also marked "OneiOS" (or "Mesa 26") in the file it is in.

air/ (the AIR frontend and air_metal):
  - Ported from Jesvi's Mesa 25.0.7 to Mesa cecc0e9 (26.3-devel, external/mesa-droidvm): the builder's `exact` is
    `fp_math_ctrl` (nir_fp_exact / nir_fp_fast_math), gl_shader_stage is mesa_shader_stage, PIPE_SHADER_* are
    MESA_SHADER_*, unreachable() is UNREACHABLE(), nir_block_create takes the impl, nir_shader_create has no
    shader_info, nir_def_rewrite_uses_after has no third argument, nir_metadata_preserve is nir_progress,
    nir_copy_prop is nir_opt_copy_prop, nir_lower_io's type_size returns unsigned; get_compute_param and
    get_compiler_options are the screen's compute_caps and nir_options[]; pipe_surface is a value (no
    create_surface: air_metal.c makes its own, rwa_surface_make), pipe->clear takes the colour and stencil masks,
    set_constant_buffer and set_sampler_views lost take_ownership.
  - air_module.c: MODULE_CODE_GUIDLIST (20), which LLVM 22 and later write, is skipped (the host test assembles its
    modules with LLVM 23; Apple's iOS 16.5 metallibs have none).
  - air_metal.c, rwa_device_open: the screen is oneios_radeonsi_screen_create() (oneios_radeonsi_screen.h, new; the
    guest Mesa stage defines it) under -Doneios-air-screen=radeonsi, where Jesvi opened freedreno (msm) or Panfrost
    over its xf86drm stand-in; without it the open fails with a sentence (RWA_SOFTWARE=1 still gives softpipe for
    tests). threadExecutionWidth is the smallest size in radeonsi's subgroup_sizes mask (32 on RDNA3, still never
    below 32).
  - meson.build (Jesvi's) unchanged; the Mesa wiring is patches/mesa/5001-air-frontend.patch (guarded subdir) and
    5002-air-metal-library.patch (src/gallium/targets/air-metal: libOneiOSRadeonAir and air_metal_test in a target of
    their own, where Jesvi declared libredwoodair in freedreno's and panfrost's meson files; options oneios-air and
    oneios-air-screen).
  - New: build.sh, host-test.sh, tests/tid_store.ll (OneiOS's own compute kernel), oneios_radeonsi_screen.h.

plugin/ (the Metal device):
  - redwoodmetal.m: the device class RedwoodMetalDevice is OneiOSRadeonMetalDevice (K3); no RedwoodGPU/RedwoodMali
    user client and no kernel GEM buffers (every buffer is Mesa's; without a screen a buffer is nil); the library is
    libOneiOSRadeonAir.dylib beside the bundle's executable (was /redwood/lib/libredwoodair.dylib); -name is Mesa's
    renderer name; linear and IOSurface alignments 256 (RDNA3's linear pitch, was Panfrost's 64); every IOSurface is
    served as a copy (Jesvi's in-place import needed its kernel's kRedwoodSurface); rm_offered: no device in
    backboardd (unless oneios-radeon-backboardd=1) and Jesvi's metaloff processes, or as OneiOSRadeonMetal.clients
    says; metal_profile= is oneios-metal-profile=; notify names com.redwood.metal.* are com.oneios.radeonmetal.*;
    error domain OneiOSRadeonMetal.
  - m2m.h: /dev/m2m (Jesvi's kernel) replaced by os_log (subsystem com.oneios.radeonmetal) and, for errors, the
    device's init and the first pipelines, the kernel's text rows (oneios-gpu-text, hosted 0039); the crash recorder
    is kept.
  - metal_plugin.plist: the K3 names (OneiOSRadeonMetal, OneiOSRadeonMetalDevice, com.oneios.radeonmetal).
  - Removed after the first commit: redwooddrawable.m (its in-place IOSurface import is its kernel's), metal_dev.m
    and metal_props.c (probes of Jesvi's kernel's services). metal_caps.m is unchanged and built as a probe.
